<title>CHINA: China rubber demand seen 1.6 mln tonnes in '97.</title>
<headline>China rubber demand seen 1.6 mln tonnes in '97.</headline>
<dateline>BEIJING 1996-12-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>China demand for rubber is estimated at 1.6 million tonnes for 1997, the China Chemical Industry News said on Monday.</p>
<p>China planned to produce 560,000 tonnes of synthetic rubber as well as 440,000 tonnes of natural rubber next year, with rubber exports planned to reach 20,000 tonnes, it said.</p>
<p>To control imports, China would import less than 500,000 tonnes of rubber in 1997, it said.</p>
<p>China's rubber output this year was expected to reach 840,000 tonnes, with natural and synthetic rubbers each accounting for half, it said.</p>
<p>Domestic demand for rubber in 1996 reached 1.48 million tonnes, far more than production, it said.</p>
</text>
